  "notes": [
    "The s24/s28 frame moves bias toward the lap to keep the pen action above its unshifted position. s29 is the dedicated clean tip insert. The s34 upward crop emphasizes the medal pocket and the two eyelines.",
    "The first take of each sound effect is already present. Optional keypad vibration is omitted so the two taps, one ring, key click, and record beep fit inside 45 frames.",
    "Existing shutter recording was measured without a slam. Layer the heavy transient from sfx_door_shut_bolt under the low-passed rattle at distance. Every part ends by frame 44 of the 75-frame shutter image; following dialogue is at least one second later.",
    "Phone treatment follows the final scripts’ twelve heard_as=phone rows, including l30 and l32. Hiss and handset voices end with l26 and a level-controlled dead tone. Use no train sound or cue suggesting a working stall.",
    "Two quiet tension entries begin when the smartphone goes into Nirala’s pocket and when the laugh begins. The second ducks at l25, falls away before l26 and resumes low under the dead-line tone. Cuts end with a hard drop and black.",
    "Cue placement and gain use the manifest envelope, accepted takes, and subtitle readability checks. Listening and full screening belong to the separate reviewer."
  ]
